1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:03,770
You can have a lot of money and live in

2
00:00:03,770 --> 00:00:06,000
fear of losing everything.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,280
And you can have little money,

4
00:00:08,280 --> 00:00:12,720
but keep great confidence in your future.

5
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:14,840
Strange, isn't it?

6
00:00:14,840 --> 00:00:17,860
Hello, and welcome to Cozy French Radio.

7
00:00:17,860 --> 00:00:18,560
It's Lia.

8
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:21,100
I'm really happy to be with you again today to

9
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:23,960
share a new moment together.

10
00:00:23,960 --> 00:00:26,430
Tell me, how are you?

11
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:27,880
Has your day been calm?

12
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:29,690
Or do you have a lot of things to

13
00:00:29,690 --> 00:00:31,720
think about right now?

14
00:00:31,720 --> 00:00:33,900
Maybe you're on public transport,

15
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:35,800
after a long day at work.

16
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:38,040
Maybe you're making your dinner.

17
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:42,280
Or maybe you've finally found a few minutes for yourself.

18
00:00:42,280 --> 00:00:44,420
This morning, while making my coffee,

19
00:00:44,420 --> 00:00:46,880
I found a little coin at the bottom

20
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:47,760
of my pocket.

21
00:00:47,760 --> 00:00:49,450
I put it on the table,

22
00:00:49,450 --> 00:00:52,200
and a question came to my mind.

23
00:00:52,250 --> 00:00:56,520
Why does money sometimes make us feel so many things?

24
00:00:56,520 --> 00:00:59,260
Joy, security,

25
00:00:59,260 --> 00:01:00,680
but also fear,

26
00:01:00,680 --> 00:01:03,720
jealousy or worry.

27
00:01:03,720 --> 00:01:07,200
It's interesting, because money is simply a tool.

28
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:10,160
And yet, the way we think about this tool

29
00:01:10,160 --> 00:01:12,960
can shape a big part of our life.

30
00:01:12,960 --> 00:01:16,290
Today, we're going to talk about two expressions you

31
00:01:16,290 --> 00:01:17,960
may have already heard:

32
00:01:17,960 --> 00:01:21,590
the rich mindset and the poor mindset.

33
00:01:21,640 --> 00:01:26,100
In French, the word "mentalité" means our usual way

34
00:01:26,100 --> 00:01:28,640
of thinking and seeing things.

35
00:01:28,640 --> 00:01:30,400
And during this conversation,

36
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:33,490
you'll be able to practise your French with simple

37
00:01:33,490 --> 00:01:37,820
examples, everyday situations and a few questions to better

38
00:01:37,820 --> 00:01:40,000
understand your own thoughts.

39
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:41,490
But before we begin,

40
00:01:41,490 --> 00:01:44,240
I'd like to make one important point clear.

41
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:49,670
Having a rich mindset doesn't automatically mean having a lot of money.

42
00:01:49,720 --> 00:01:52,610
And having little money absolutely doesn't mean

43
00:01:52,610 --> 00:01:54,760
having a bad mindset.

44
00:01:54,760 --> 00:01:58,560
Our financial situations depend on many things:

45
00:01:58,560 --> 00:02:00,780
our family, our health,

46
00:02:00,780 --> 00:02:04,780
our work, the opportunities we've come across and

47
00:02:04,780 --> 00:02:07,040
sometimes simply luck.

48
00:02:07,040 --> 00:02:11,240
So today, we're not going to judge rich or poor people.

49
00:02:11,240 --> 00:02:14,510
Instead, we'll explore two ways of thinking:

50
00:02:14,560 --> 00:02:17,410
a mindset that stays locked in fear and

51
00:02:17,410 --> 00:02:22,000
a mindset that looks for possibilities, even small ones.

52
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,440
Now imagine two people.

53
00:02:24,440 --> 00:02:26,360
The first one is called Thomas.

54
00:02:26,360 --> 00:02:28,520
Thomas earns a very good living.

55
00:02:28,520 --> 00:02:30,640
He owns a beautiful house,

56
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:33,840
a new car and several expensive things.

57
00:02:33,840 --> 00:02:36,880
From the outside, his life looks perfect.

58
00:02:36,880 --> 00:02:41,320
But every evening, he checks his bank account with worry.

59
00:02:41,320 --> 00:02:43,750
He constantly compares himself to others.

60
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:46,320
When a colleague buys a more expensive car,

61
00:02:46,320 --> 00:02:48,400
Thomas feels less important.

62
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:50,580
When a friend gets a promotion,

63
00:02:50,580 --> 00:02:52,960
he feels like he's losing his place.

64
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:55,130
He owns a lot of things,

65
00:02:55,130 --> 00:02:58,040
but he never feels he has enough.

66
00:02:58,040 --> 00:03:00,240
Now, imagine Sophie.

67
00:03:00,240 --> 00:03:02,600
Sophie has a more modest salary.

68
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:05,170
She has to be careful with her spending and she

69
00:03:05,170 --> 00:03:07,440
can't buy everything she wants.

70
00:03:07,440 --> 00:03:10,190
Sometimes, she worries about the future.

71
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:12,840
But she tries to build a life that fits

72
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:13,760
her needs.

73
00:03:13,760 --> 00:03:17,120
She learns new things when she has the chance.

74
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:19,960
She enjoys simple moments with her loved ones.

75
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:22,140
And she doesn't measure her whole worth by

76
00:03:22,140 --> 00:03:23,440
what she owns.

77
00:03:23,440 --> 00:03:24,600
So, tell me…

78
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:26,720
Who really feels rich?

79
00:03:26,720 --> 00:03:29,210
Thomas has more money.

80
00:03:29,210 --> 00:03:32,480
But Sophie seems to have more peace of mind.

81
00:03:32,480 --> 00:03:36,470
Of course, that doesn't mean money isn't important.

82
00:03:36,520 --> 00:03:39,600
Having enough money for housing,

83
00:03:39,600 --> 00:03:43,890
food, healthcare and living without constant worry can

84
00:03:43,890 --> 00:03:46,040
make a huge difference.

85
00:03:46,040 --> 00:03:48,560
But here's an idea to keep in mind.

86
00:03:48,560 --> 00:03:51,360
Money can improve your living conditions.

87
00:03:51,360 --> 00:03:52,650
It doesn't decide,

88
00:03:52,650 --> 00:03:56,080
on its own, how you look at your life.

89
00:03:56,080 --> 00:03:59,100
And maybe the first kind of wealth begins

90
00:03:59,100 --> 00:04:02,590
with this question: "Am I trying to build

91
00:04:02,590 --> 00:04:03,660
a life that suits me…

92
00:04:03,660 --> 00:04:06,920
or simply a life that impresses others?"

93
00:04:06,920 --> 00:04:10,280
There are two questions that can change our

94
00:04:10,280 --> 00:04:13,120
way of reacting to a difficulty.

95
00:04:13,120 --> 00:04:18,320
The first is: "Why is this happening to me?"

96
00:04:18,320 --> 00:04:24,120
The second is: "What can I do now?"

97
00:04:24,120 --> 00:04:27,350
These two questions can come up in the same situation.

98
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:30,480
But they don't always lead us in the same direction.

99
00:04:30,480 --> 00:04:34,400
Imagine two colleagues who work in a small shop.

100
00:04:34,400 --> 00:04:37,920
One Monday morning, the manager announces some bad news.

101
00:04:37,920 --> 00:04:40,680
The shop is selling fewer products than before.

102
00:04:40,680 --> 00:04:43,240
The company has to cut some costs,

103
00:04:43,240 --> 00:04:46,120
and working hours might change.

104
00:04:46,120 --> 00:04:47,910
The two colleagues are worried.

105
00:04:47,910 --> 00:04:48,840
That's normal.

106
00:04:48,840 --> 00:04:52,230
They need their salary to pay their bills.

107
00:04:52,280 --> 00:04:54,440
The first person, Marc,

108
00:04:54,440 --> 00:04:57,720
goes home feeling very angry.

109
00:04:57,720 --> 00:05:00,520
He tells himself: "It's always the same.

110
00:05:00,520 --> 00:05:02,720
Nothing ever works out for me.

111
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:04,760
I'm just really unlucky."

112
00:05:04,760 --> 00:05:08,240
For several days, he only thinks about the worst.

113
00:05:08,240 --> 00:05:10,480
He imagines losing his job.

114
00:05:10,480 --> 00:05:13,280
He imagines no longer being able to pay his rent.

115
00:05:13,280 --> 00:05:16,080
And the more he thinks about these possibilities,

116
00:05:16,080 --> 00:05:18,470
the more powerless he feels.

117
00:05:18,520 --> 00:05:20,590
The second person, Claire,

118
00:05:20,590 --> 00:05:23,280
feels exactly the same worry.

119
00:05:23,280 --> 00:05:24,590
She's scared too.

120
00:05:24,590 --> 00:05:27,040
She's thinking about her bills too.

121
00:05:27,040 --> 00:05:28,560
But after a few days,

122
00:05:28,560 --> 00:05:31,200
she decides to look at what she can do.

123
00:05:31,200 --> 00:05:35,480
She talks with her manager to better understand the situation.

124
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:37,270
She updates her CV.

125
00:05:37,270 --> 00:05:40,560
She looks for information about free training courses.

126
00:05:40,560 --> 00:05:44,710
And she starts thinking about other career options.

127
00:05:44,760 --> 00:05:47,010
Claire doesn't know if everything will be fine.

128
00:05:47,010 --> 00:05:48,760
She has no guarantee.

129
00:05:48,760 --> 00:05:51,920
But she tries to get back a small part of

130
00:05:51,920 --> 00:05:53,480
her power to act.

131
00:05:53,480 --> 00:05:55,080
Do you see the difference?

132
00:05:55,080 --> 00:05:57,890
It's not that Claire is braver or

133
00:05:57,890 --> 00:05:59,160
better than Marc.

134
00:05:59,160 --> 00:06:02,330
They simply don't react the same way

135
00:06:02,330 --> 00:06:03,600
at that particular moment.

136
00:06:03,600 --> 00:06:06,400
And it's important to understand that we can

137
00:06:06,400 --> 00:06:09,040
all be like Marc on some days.

138
00:06:09,040 --> 00:06:11,220
When we're exhausted,

139
00:06:11,220 --> 00:06:15,840
worried or discouraged, it becomes hard to imagine solutions.

140
00:06:15,840 --> 00:06:18,600
So we shouldn't judge ourselves too quickly.

141
00:06:18,600 --> 00:06:21,480
But there's an interesting idea.

142
00:06:21,480 --> 00:06:24,760
We can't always choose what happens to us.

143
00:06:24,760 --> 00:06:28,300
We can sometimes choose the next small step

144
00:06:28,300 --> 00:06:29,840
we're going to take.

145
00:06:29,840 --> 00:06:32,360
And that step can be very simple.

146
00:06:32,360 --> 00:06:33,720
Asking a question.

147
00:06:33,720 --> 00:06:35,040
Asking for help.

148
00:06:35,040 --> 00:06:36,880
Looking for some information.

149
00:06:36,880 --> 00:06:41,710
Or taking a few minutes to think before making a decision.

150
00:06:41,760 --> 00:06:45,500
Sometimes, we think a rich mindset means taking

151
00:06:45,500 --> 00:06:46,800
big risks.

152
00:06:46,800 --> 00:06:48,980
Investing a lot of money.

153
00:06:48,980 --> 00:06:50,800
Starting a business.

154
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:53,400
Never being afraid of failure.

155
00:06:53,400 --> 00:06:55,640
But that picture is too simple.

156
00:06:55,640 --> 00:06:59,840
Some people can't take big financial risks.

157
00:06:59,840 --> 00:07:01,520
When you have to pay your rent,

158
00:07:01,520 --> 00:07:04,320
feed your family or pay back a debt,

159
00:07:04,320 --> 00:07:06,920
caution can be necessary.

160
00:07:06,920 --> 00:07:09,830
And being careful isn't a weakness.

161
00:07:09,880 --> 00:07:12,160
So the real question isn't:

162
00:07:12,160 --> 00:07:14,600
"Am I ready to risk everything?"

163
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:20,000
But rather: "What realistic options exist in my situation?"

164
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:23,320
Maybe you can't change jobs right away.

165
00:07:23,320 --> 00:07:25,040
But you can find out more.

166
00:07:25,040 --> 00:07:28,280
Maybe you can't pay for an expensive course.

167
00:07:28,280 --> 00:07:30,880
But you can find free resources.

168
00:07:30,880 --> 00:07:33,880
Maybe you can't save this month.

169
00:07:33,880 --> 00:07:36,880
But you can try to better understand your spending,

170
00:07:36,880 --> 00:07:38,750
without feeling guilty.

171
00:07:38,800 --> 00:07:42,480
Change sometimes starts with a new piece of information.

172
00:07:42,480 --> 00:07:45,800
And that information can open up a possibility.

173
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:50,040
You know, we tend to imagine two kinds of people.

174
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:51,760
Those who succeed.

175
00:07:51,760 --> 00:07:53,360
And those who fail.

176
00:07:53,360 --> 00:07:56,120
But life is much more complex.

177
00:07:56,120 --> 00:07:58,800
We all go through different periods.

178
00:07:58,800 --> 00:08:00,560
Sometimes, we move forward.

179
00:08:00,560 --> 00:08:03,560
Sometimes, we simply have to hold on.

180
00:08:03,560 --> 00:08:07,450
And sometimes, the best progress is recognising that

181
00:08:07,450 --> 00:08:09,400
we need support.

182
00:08:09,400 --> 00:08:15,560
So, if you're going through money or work troubles, remember this.

183
00:08:15,560 --> 00:08:19,600
Your current situation doesn't define your whole worth.

184
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:21,360
You are not your salary.

185
00:08:21,360 --> 00:08:23,440
You are not your bank account.

186
00:08:23,440 --> 00:08:25,870
And you're not a bad person because

187
00:08:25,870 --> 00:08:27,800
you're having difficulties.

188
00:08:27,800 --> 00:08:30,280
You're a human being trying to build

189
00:08:30,280 --> 00:08:33,110
your life with the means you have.

190
00:08:33,160 --> 00:08:37,120
And sometimes, asking a new question is already a

191
00:08:37,120 --> 00:08:39,840
way to start moving forward.

192
00:08:39,840 --> 00:08:44,320
Sometimes, we buy things we don't really need…

193
00:08:44,320 --> 00:08:49,120
to impress people whose opinion we don't even know.

194
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:50,800
That might sound funny.

195
00:08:50,800 --> 00:08:53,120
But think about it for a moment.

196
00:08:53,120 --> 00:08:57,280
How many times have we wanted something simply because

197
00:08:57,280 --> 00:08:59,590
someone else had it?

198
00:08:59,640 --> 00:09:01,610
A new phone.

199
00:09:01,610 --> 00:09:02,340
A watch.

200
00:09:02,340 --> 00:09:03,480
A car.

201
00:09:03,480 --> 00:09:05,600
Clothes from a famous brand.

202
00:09:05,600 --> 00:09:09,120
Or even a holiday in a popular place.

203
00:09:09,120 --> 00:09:12,240
Imagine a young woman called Julie.

204
00:09:12,240 --> 00:09:14,160
Julie works in an office.

205
00:09:14,160 --> 00:09:17,320
She earns enough to pay her usual expenses,

206
00:09:17,320 --> 00:09:20,040
but she has to be careful with her budget.

207
00:09:20,040 --> 00:09:23,800
One day, several colleagues show up with new phones.

208
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:25,480
They talk about the cameras,

209
00:09:25,480 --> 00:09:28,350
the screens and the new features.

210
00:09:28,400 --> 00:09:30,600
Julie listens to the conversation.

211
00:09:30,600 --> 00:09:32,960
Her phone still works very well.

212
00:09:32,960 --> 00:09:37,280
She can call, send messages and take photos.

213
00:09:37,280 --> 00:09:40,800
But suddenly, she starts to find it old.

214
00:09:40,800 --> 00:09:43,640
She looks at her colleagues' phones and thinks:

215
00:09:43,640 --> 00:09:46,320
"Maybe I should buy a new one."

216
00:09:46,320 --> 00:09:49,840
In the evening, she looks up prices online.

217
00:09:49,840 --> 00:09:52,880
The model she likes is very expensive.

218
00:09:52,880 --> 00:09:55,110
She could buy it in several instalments.

219
00:09:55,160 --> 00:09:58,720
But that would cut the money left for other needs.

220
00:09:58,720 --> 00:10:00,840
So she hesitates.

221
00:10:00,840 --> 00:10:03,240
And a question comes to her mind.

222
00:10:03,240 --> 00:10:05,840
"Do I really want this phone…

223
00:10:05,840 --> 00:10:08,500
or do I just want to have the same one

224
00:10:08,500 --> 00:10:09,560
as everyone else?"

225
00:10:09,560 --> 00:10:12,160
That question changes something.

226
00:10:12,160 --> 00:10:16,440
Julie realises her desire isn't only about the object.

227
00:10:16,440 --> 00:10:19,000
She'd also like to feel accepted.

228
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:22,590
She'd like not to feel different.

229
00:10:22,640 --> 00:10:25,600
And you know, that wish is very human.

230
00:10:25,600 --> 00:10:28,200
We all want to belong to a group.

231
00:10:28,200 --> 00:10:29,960
We like being appreciated.

232
00:10:29,960 --> 00:10:33,080
We sometimes like to show that our life is moving forward.

233
00:10:33,080 --> 00:10:35,480
There's nothing shameful about that.

234
00:10:35,480 --> 00:10:39,040
But the problem starts when we use our money

235
00:10:39,040 --> 00:10:42,280
to buy an image of ourselves that doesn't match

236
00:10:42,280 --> 00:10:44,440
our real needs.

237
00:10:44,440 --> 00:10:48,440
Because that image often demands new purchases.

238
00:10:48,440 --> 00:10:51,830
After the phone, maybe there'll be a watch.

239
00:10:51,880 --> 00:10:54,320
After the watch, a car.

240
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:57,320
After the car, something else.

241
00:10:57,320 --> 00:10:59,920
And we can spend a lot of time chasing

242
00:10:59,920 --> 00:11:04,640
a feeling of success that quickly fades.

243
00:11:04,640 --> 00:11:06,520
Here's the paradox.

244
00:11:06,520 --> 00:11:09,600
The more we try to prove we're rich,

245
00:11:09,600 --> 00:11:14,240
the more we sometimes risk losing our financial freedom.

246
00:11:14,240 --> 00:11:17,680
Of course, buying nice things isn't bad.

247
00:11:17,680 --> 00:11:19,120
If you love something,

248
00:11:19,120 --> 00:11:21,270
if you can afford it and if it

249
00:11:21,270 --> 00:11:25,120
makes you happy, you have every right to buy it.

250
00:11:25,120 --> 00:11:27,250
The problem isn't pleasure.

251
00:11:27,250 --> 00:11:28,840
It's pressure.

252
00:11:28,840 --> 00:11:30,720
That little voice that says:

253
00:11:30,720 --> 00:11:32,180
"If I don't have this,

254
00:11:32,180 --> 00:11:34,520
I'm worth less than others."

255
00:11:34,520 --> 00:11:37,360
But your worth doesn't depend on your phone.

256
00:11:37,360 --> 00:11:39,640
It doesn't depend on your car.

257
00:11:39,640 --> 00:11:43,200
And it doesn't depend on the price of your clothes either.

258
00:11:43,200 --> 00:11:46,080
Now imagine another scene.

259
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:48,860
Two friends meet up in a café.

260
00:11:48,910 --> 00:11:52,440
One says he's just bought a very expensive car.

261
00:11:52,440 --> 00:11:55,940
The other explains he's decided to keep his old

262
00:11:55,940 --> 00:12:00,440
car to save up for a personal project.

263
00:12:00,440 --> 00:12:03,720
Neither choice is automatically better.

264
00:12:03,720 --> 00:12:05,800
It all depends on their situation,

265
00:12:05,800 --> 00:12:08,600
their needs and their priorities.

266
00:12:08,600 --> 00:12:12,480
But the second friend seems very calm about his decision.

267
00:12:12,480 --> 00:12:14,920
He's not trying to convince anyone.

268
00:12:14,920 --> 00:12:17,430
He knows why he's making this choice.

269
00:12:17,480 --> 00:12:20,440
And that calm is precious.

270
00:12:20,440 --> 00:12:25,800
Because financial freedom doesn't necessarily mean becoming a millionaire.

271
00:12:25,800 --> 00:12:29,810
It can also mean having enough room to

272
00:12:29,810 --> 00:12:33,360
make some choices without constant pressure.

273
00:12:33,360 --> 00:12:36,280
Being able to say no to a useless expense.

274
00:12:36,280 --> 00:12:38,470
Being able to handle the unexpected,

275
00:12:38,470 --> 00:12:40,480
when our means allow it.

276
00:12:40,480 --> 00:12:43,640
Or being able to choose something that makes us happy,

277
00:12:43,640 --> 00:12:46,670
even if it impresses no one.

278
00:12:46,720 --> 00:12:49,760
So, the next time you feel like buying

279
00:12:49,760 --> 00:12:53,640
something, you can ask yourself a very simple question.

280
00:12:53,640 --> 00:12:55,960
"If no one saw this object,

281
00:12:55,960 --> 00:12:58,400
would I still want to buy it?"

282
00:12:58,400 --> 00:13:01,200
If the answer is yes, great.

283
00:13:01,200 --> 00:13:03,040
But if the answer is no,

284
00:13:03,040 --> 00:13:06,200
maybe you've just discovered something interesting

285
00:13:06,200 --> 00:13:07,840
about your desire.

286
00:13:07,840 --> 00:13:11,680
And sometimes, understanding what we really want

287
00:13:11,680 --> 00:13:15,590
gives us more freedom than owning a new object.

288
00:13:15,640 --> 00:13:18,860
A big difference in our life can sometimes start

289
00:13:18,860 --> 00:13:24,000
with a habit so small that nobody notices it.

290
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:27,320
Imagine a man called Nicolas.

291
00:13:27,320 --> 00:13:29,280
Nicolas works in a restaurant.

292
00:13:29,280 --> 00:13:30,840
He likes his job,

293
00:13:30,840 --> 00:13:33,440
but one day he'd like to get a position with

294
00:13:33,440 --> 00:13:35,960
more responsibility.

295
00:13:35,960 --> 00:13:38,880
He knows he needs to improve some skills.

296
00:13:38,880 --> 00:13:41,600
But he doesn't have much time.

297
00:13:41,600 --> 00:13:43,430
In the morning, he leaves early.

298
00:13:43,480 --> 00:13:45,960
In the evening, he comes home tired.

299
00:13:45,960 --> 00:13:48,640
And when he thinks about a full training course,

300
00:13:48,640 --> 00:13:51,880
it seems impossible.

301
00:13:51,880 --> 00:13:56,240
So, one day, he decides to start differently.

302
00:13:56,240 --> 00:13:58,360
Every morning, on his commute,

303
00:13:58,360 --> 00:14:00,720
he listens to ten minutes of English.

304
00:14:00,720 --> 00:14:01,880
Not an hour.

305
00:14:01,880 --> 00:14:03,560
Not a complicated programme.

306
00:14:03,560 --> 00:14:06,360
Just ten minutes.

307
00:14:06,360 --> 00:14:08,720
At first, he understands very little.

308
00:14:08,720 --> 00:14:10,520
Some words are hard.

309
00:14:10,520 --> 00:14:12,990
Some sentences are too fast.

310
00:14:13,040 --> 00:14:15,840
But he keeps going when he can.

311
00:14:15,840 --> 00:14:19,720
After a few weeks, he recognises more expressions.

312
00:14:19,720 --> 00:14:23,320
After several months, he starts using a few phrases

313
00:14:23,320 --> 00:14:25,520
with foreign customers.

314
00:14:25,520 --> 00:14:29,440
And one day, his manager notices his progress.

315
00:14:29,440 --> 00:14:34,840
He asks him to help more with welcoming international guests.

316
00:14:34,840 --> 00:14:37,200
It's not a magical transformation.

317
00:14:37,200 --> 00:14:40,550
Nicolas didn't become bilingual in a few weeks.

318
00:14:40,600 --> 00:14:43,820
But he developed a useful skill thanks to

319
00:14:43,820 --> 00:14:45,600
a small habit.

320
00:14:45,600 --> 00:14:50,080
And that skill gives him new opportunities.

321
00:14:50,080 --> 00:14:51,640
I really love this story,

322
00:14:51,640 --> 00:14:53,760
because it reminds us of one thing.

323
00:14:53,760 --> 00:14:58,520
We sometimes overestimate what we can achieve in one day.

324
00:14:58,520 --> 00:15:02,050
And we underestimate what we can build with

325
00:15:02,050 --> 00:15:04,640
small, repeated efforts.

326
00:15:04,640 --> 00:15:08,430
This can also apply to our relationship with money.

327
00:15:08,480 --> 00:15:11,560
Imagine someone who decides to write down their spending

328
00:15:11,560 --> 00:15:12,920
for a month.

329
00:15:12,920 --> 00:15:14,560
Not to criticise themselves.

330
00:15:14,560 --> 00:15:17,000
Not to stop all the little pleasures.

331
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:19,720
Just to understand.

332
00:15:19,720 --> 00:15:23,580
They discover they regularly spend money on certain

333
00:15:23,580 --> 00:15:25,760
things they hardly use.

334
00:15:25,760 --> 00:15:29,280
So they decide to change one habit.

335
00:15:29,280 --> 00:15:31,440
They cancel a useless subscription.

336
00:15:31,440 --> 00:15:34,760
Or they sometimes make their lunch at home.

337
00:15:34,760 --> 00:15:36,870
And if their situation allows it,

338
00:15:36,920 --> 00:15:39,480
they put a small amount aside.

339
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:41,400
It may not be much.

340
00:15:41,400 --> 00:15:45,160
But they start to better understand where their money goes.

341
00:15:45,160 --> 00:15:49,680
And that knowledge gives them a little more confidence.

342
00:15:49,680 --> 00:15:52,560
Of course, we have to stay realistic.

343
00:15:52,560 --> 00:15:55,950
Some people have such limited incomes that they

344
00:15:55,950 --> 00:15:58,200
can save almost nothing.

345
00:15:58,200 --> 00:16:02,320
In that case, the problem isn't simply a bad habit.

346
00:16:02,320 --> 00:16:04,590
It may be linked to the cost of living,

347
00:16:04,640 --> 00:16:08,680
wage levels or heavy responsibilities.

348
00:16:08,680 --> 00:16:11,390
And no one should be ashamed of not

349
00:16:11,390 --> 00:16:14,160
being able to put money aside.

350
00:16:14,160 --> 00:16:16,920
But even when our options are limited,

351
00:16:16,920 --> 00:16:21,010
learning to better understand our situation can help us

352
00:16:21,010 --> 00:16:23,200
make certain decisions.

353
00:16:23,200 --> 00:16:26,720
That's what a future-oriented mindset is.

354
00:16:26,720 --> 00:16:29,880
Not thinking everything is possible right away.

355
00:16:29,880 --> 00:16:32,440
But looking for what can be improved,

356
00:16:32,440 --> 00:16:34,470
at our own pace.

357
00:16:34,520 --> 00:16:37,320
You know, there's a difference between saying:

358
00:16:37,320 --> 00:16:39,760
"I have to get rich fast."

359
00:16:39,760 --> 00:16:43,480
And saying: "I want to build a slightly

360
00:16:43,480 --> 00:16:45,920
more stable situation over time."

361
00:16:45,920 --> 00:16:48,960
The first sentence can create a lot of pressure.

362
00:16:48,960 --> 00:16:53,840
The second can help us move forward with more patience.

363
00:16:53,840 --> 00:16:56,480
And patience matters.

364
00:16:56,480 --> 00:17:00,680
Because results aren't always visible right away.

365
00:17:00,680 --> 00:17:02,270
When you learn a language,

366
00:17:02,320 --> 00:17:05,560
you don't necessarily notice your progress every day.

367
00:17:05,560 --> 00:17:07,520
When you develop a skill,

368
00:17:07,520 --> 00:17:11,040
you don't always get an immediate reward.

369
00:17:11,040 --> 00:17:13,600
And when you try to manage your budget better,

370
00:17:13,600 --> 00:17:17,800
it sometimes takes time before you feel a difference.

371
00:17:17,800 --> 00:17:21,360
But that doesn't mean your efforts are useless.

372
00:17:21,360 --> 00:17:25,420
Sometimes, they're simply building something you

373
00:17:25,420 --> 00:17:26,840
can't see yet.

374
00:17:26,840 --> 00:17:31,310
Like a plant growing its roots before it grows tall.

375
00:17:31,360 --> 00:17:33,200
So don't only ask yourself:

376
00:17:33,200 --> 00:17:36,000
"What can I get today?"

377
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:39,910
Also ask yourself: "What habit could make my life

378
00:17:39,910 --> 00:17:42,720
a little easier in six months?"

379
00:17:42,720 --> 00:17:45,720
The answer doesn't need to be impressive.

380
00:17:45,720 --> 00:17:48,960
It just needs to fit your life.

381
00:17:48,960 --> 00:17:52,700
Because a small, realistic habit is often worth more than a

382
00:17:52,700 --> 00:17:56,000
big project you can't keep up.

383
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:58,960
What if the secret to a rich life wasn't

384
00:17:58,960 --> 00:18:01,030
always owning more…

385
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:05,320
but knowing what is enough for you?

386
00:18:05,320 --> 00:18:07,200
It's a simple question.

387
00:18:07,200 --> 00:18:11,520
And yet, it can change our relationship with money.

388
00:18:11,520 --> 00:18:14,600
Imagine a man called Antoine.

389
00:18:14,600 --> 00:18:17,760
For a long time, Antoine thought happiness would come

390
00:18:17,760 --> 00:18:19,920
when he had a better salary.

391
00:18:19,920 --> 00:18:21,560
So he worked.

392
00:18:21,560 --> 00:18:23,360
He got a promotion.

393
00:18:23,360 --> 00:18:25,520
His salary went up.

394
00:18:25,520 --> 00:18:28,470
For a few weeks, he was very happy.

395
00:18:28,520 --> 00:18:32,080
But soon, he started thinking about something else.

396
00:18:32,080 --> 00:18:33,760
A bigger apartment.

397
00:18:33,760 --> 00:18:35,440
A newer car.

398
00:18:35,440 --> 00:18:38,000
More expensive holidays.

399
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:40,760
So he set himself new goals.

400
00:18:40,760 --> 00:18:42,280
And when he reached them,

401
00:18:42,280 --> 00:18:44,800
other wants appeared.

402
00:18:44,800 --> 00:18:48,120
One evening, he comes home after a long day.

403
00:18:48,120 --> 00:18:49,880
He sits down in his living room.

404
00:18:49,880 --> 00:18:52,760
Around him, there are lots of beautiful things.

405
00:18:52,760 --> 00:18:54,710
But he feels tired.

406
00:18:54,760 --> 00:18:56,920
He realises he spends almost all his time

407
00:18:56,920 --> 00:19:00,840
working to pay for a life he barely enjoys.

408
00:19:00,840 --> 00:19:02,560
And for the first time,

409
00:19:02,560 --> 00:19:05,360
he asks himself a different question.

410
00:19:05,360 --> 00:19:09,320
"How much do I really need to live well?"

411
00:19:09,320 --> 00:19:11,200
It's not an easy question.

412
00:19:11,200 --> 00:19:13,880
Because we don't all have the same needs.

413
00:19:13,880 --> 00:19:16,360
A person with children doesn't have the same

414
00:19:16,360 --> 00:19:19,360
responsibilities as someone who lives alone.

415
00:19:19,360 --> 00:19:22,070
A person who has to help their family may

416
00:19:22,070 --> 00:19:25,200
need more financial security.

417
00:19:25,200 --> 00:19:27,880
And a person going through health problems

418
00:19:27,880 --> 00:19:30,680
may have big expenses.

419
00:19:30,680 --> 00:19:33,840
So there's no magic amount that represents

420
00:19:33,840 --> 00:19:36,120
wealth for everyone.

421
00:19:36,120 --> 00:19:38,880
But we can try to define what

422
00:19:38,880 --> 00:19:42,000
"enough" means in our own life.

423
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:44,680
Enough to live in a safe place.

424
00:19:44,680 --> 00:19:47,080
Enough to eat properly.

425
00:19:47,080 --> 00:19:49,870
Enough to take care of your health.

426
00:19:49,920 --> 00:19:52,640
Enough to face some difficulties.

427
00:19:52,640 --> 00:19:57,360
And, if possible, enough to enjoy a few simple pleasures.

428
00:19:57,360 --> 00:20:00,600
Of course, wanting to earn more money isn't bad.

429
00:20:00,600 --> 00:20:03,880
Money can bring important opportunities.

430
00:20:03,880 --> 00:20:06,400
It can help us support our family,

431
00:20:06,400 --> 00:20:09,880
discover the world or prepare for our future.

432
00:20:09,880 --> 00:20:12,680
But there's a difference between wanting to improve

433
00:20:12,680 --> 00:20:15,300
your life and believing your life will only have

434
00:20:15,300 --> 00:20:19,310
value once you've reached a certain level of wealth.

435
00:20:19,360 --> 00:20:22,570
You can have ambition without spending every day

436
00:20:22,570 --> 00:20:24,400
feeling not good enough.

437
00:20:24,400 --> 00:20:29,040
You can want more without looking down on what you already have.

438
00:20:29,040 --> 00:20:31,620
And you can be proud of your progress without

439
00:20:31,620 --> 00:20:34,760
constantly comparing yourself to others.

440
00:20:34,760 --> 00:20:37,960
I'd like to tell you one last little scene.

441
00:20:37,960 --> 00:20:40,760
An elderly woman is sitting in her garden.

442
00:20:40,760 --> 00:20:43,720
She's drinking tea and looking at the flowers.

443
00:20:43,720 --> 00:20:45,860
Her grandson asks her:

444
00:20:45,910 --> 00:20:49,390
"Grandma, if you could have much more money,

445
00:20:49,390 --> 00:20:51,120
what would you buy?"

446
00:20:51,120 --> 00:20:53,310
She thinks for a moment.

447
00:20:53,310 --> 00:20:57,760
Then she answers: "Maybe a slightly bigger garden."

448
00:20:57,760 --> 00:20:59,600
Her grandson smiles.

449
00:20:59,600 --> 00:21:01,390
"And then?"

450
00:21:01,390 --> 00:21:03,920
She looks at the flowers in front of her.

451
00:21:03,920 --> 00:21:04,640
"Then…

452
00:21:04,640 --> 00:21:08,680
I think I'd come back here to drink my tea."

453
00:21:08,680 --> 00:21:10,820
That answer is funny,

454
00:21:10,820 --> 00:21:12,630
but it holds a truth.

455
00:21:12,680 --> 00:21:15,920
Sometimes, we imagine we need to own much more

456
00:21:15,920 --> 00:21:20,000
to live moments we can already enjoy today.

457
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:23,000
Of course, that doesn't mean money troubles

458
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:26,480
disappear with a good attitude.

459
00:21:26,480 --> 00:21:29,680
When someone lacks money for their basic needs,

460
00:21:29,680 --> 00:21:31,870
they need concrete solutions,

461
00:21:31,870 --> 00:21:34,480
not just positive thoughts.

462
00:21:34,480 --> 00:21:37,110
But when we have a little stability,

463
00:21:37,160 --> 00:21:40,260
we can also learn to recognise what truly

464
00:21:40,260 --> 00:21:42,680
brings us satisfaction.

465
00:21:42,680 --> 00:21:45,040
And maybe the rich mindset,

466
00:21:45,040 --> 00:21:48,480
in its deepest sense, begins here.

467
00:21:48,480 --> 00:21:52,220
With the ability to tell what truly improves

468
00:21:52,220 --> 00:21:55,770
our life from what only gives us the feeling

469
00:21:55,770 --> 00:21:57,360
of being more important.

470
00:21:57,360 --> 00:22:00,230
Because wealth isn't measured only

471
00:22:00,230 --> 00:22:01,360
in numbers.

472
00:22:01,360 --> 00:22:03,560
It can also be seen in the time

473
00:22:03,560 --> 00:22:06,190
we have for the people we love.

474
00:22:06,240 --> 00:22:09,080
In our ability to make some choices.

475
00:22:09,080 --> 00:22:11,040
In our peace of mind.

476
00:22:11,040 --> 00:22:13,910
And in the feeling of living a life that

477
00:22:13,910 --> 00:22:16,080
matches our values.

478
00:22:16,080 --> 00:22:19,100
So, today, I'm not going to ask you if

479
00:22:19,100 --> 00:22:20,720
you want to become rich.

480
00:22:20,720 --> 00:22:23,880
Instead, I'd like to ask you another question.

481
00:22:23,880 --> 00:22:27,880
If you had enough money to live without worry,

482
00:22:27,880 --> 00:22:31,200
what would you like to spend your days doing?

483
00:22:31,200 --> 00:22:34,830
Your answer could teach you something very important.

484
00:22:34,880 --> 00:22:37,360
Not only about your relationship with money.

485
00:22:37,360 --> 00:22:41,720
But also about the life you truly want to build.

486
00:22:41,720 --> 00:22:43,040
Before we say goodbye,

487
00:22:43,040 --> 00:22:46,320
I'd like you to keep one last thought.

488
00:22:46,320 --> 00:22:50,800
You don't need a lot of money to deserve respect.

489
00:22:50,800 --> 00:22:53,990
You don't need to impress others to have

490
00:22:53,990 --> 00:22:54,760
value.

491
00:22:54,760 --> 00:22:57,920
And you don't need to turn every minute

492
00:22:57,920 --> 00:23:01,700
of your life into a chance to earn more.

493
00:23:01,750 --> 00:23:03,290
Money is important.

494
00:23:03,290 --> 00:23:04,680
It helps us live,

495
00:23:04,680 --> 00:23:08,200
protect ourselves and build certain projects.

496
00:23:08,200 --> 00:23:13,000
But it's not the only measure of a good life.

497
00:23:13,000 --> 00:23:17,800
Maybe today, your financial situation isn't the one you want.

498
00:23:17,800 --> 00:23:19,960
Maybe you work a lot.

499
00:23:19,960 --> 00:23:22,510
Maybe you're just trying to find a little

500
00:23:22,510 --> 00:23:24,240
more stability.

501
00:23:24,240 --> 00:23:27,160
So go at your own pace.

502
00:23:27,160 --> 00:23:28,920
Learn what you can.

503
00:23:28,920 --> 00:23:31,510
Ask for help when you need it.

504
00:23:31,560 --> 00:23:37,120
And remember that your difficulties don't define your worth.

505
00:23:37,120 --> 00:23:40,360
You can want to improve your situation while respecting

506
00:23:40,360 --> 00:23:43,000
the person you are today.

507
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:45,480
Thank you for spending this moment with me.

508
00:23:45,480 --> 00:23:48,410
I hope this conversation helped you practise your

509
00:23:48,410 --> 00:23:52,120
French and think a little differently about money,

510
00:23:52,120 --> 00:23:55,400
success and happiness.

511
00:23:55,400 --> 00:23:59,030
Before you go, I'd like to ask you a question.

512
00:23:59,080 --> 00:24:04,640
For you, what does being rich really mean?

513
00:24:04,640 --> 00:24:07,120
Is it having a lot of money,

514
00:24:07,120 --> 00:24:09,960
free time, security,

515
00:24:09,960 --> 00:24:11,960
or something else?

516
00:24:11,960 --> 00:24:14,630
Have you ever had an experience that changed the

517
00:24:14,630 --> 00:24:16,640
way you think about money?

518
00:24:16,640 --> 00:24:18,430
Tell me in the comments.

519
00:24:18,430 --> 00:24:21,200
I'd be very happy to read you.

520
00:24:21,200 --> 00:24:23,240
Take good care of yourself, my friend.

521
00:24:23,240 --> 00:24:26,920
See you very soon on Cozy French Radio.

522
00:24:26,920 --> 00:24:29,640
See you soon.
